        "id": "E2",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Can AI help scientists identify promising drug candidates?",
        "sourceUrl": "https://openai.com/index/introducing-medchembench",
        "source": "OpenAI",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-20T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-22T17:48:44.944Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E3",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Building AI that can reliably support this work is one step towards helping scientists develop better medicines.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://openai.com/index/introducing-medchembench",
        "source": "OpenAI",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-20T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-22T17:48:44.944Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E4",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "For AI to help, it needs to connect changes in molecular structure with experimental evidence and reason about what compounds are worth pursuing.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://openai.com/index/introducing-medchembench",
        "source": "OpenAI",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-20T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-22T17:48:44.944Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E5",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "MedChemBench measures these abilities through 99 problems drawn from published research.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://openai.com/index/introducing-medchembench",
        "source": "OpenAI",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-20T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-22T17:48:44.944Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E6",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "At the xhigh reasoning setting, GPT‑6.2 Astra earned 84.5% of the available credit, compared with 83.3% for GPT‑6 Astra, 82.0% for GPT‑6.1 Sol, and 58.2% for GPT‑5.6 Sol.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://openai.com/index/introducing-medchembench",
        "source": "OpenAI",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-20T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-22T17:48:44.944Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E7",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "GPT‑6 Astra was strongest at reconstructing molecular structures and explaining experimental evidence.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://openai.com/index/introducing-medchembench",
        "source": "OpenAI",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-20T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-22T17:48:44.944Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E8",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "One MedChemBench problem draws on research into inhibitors of PRMT5, a protein studied in cancer drug discovery.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://openai.com/index/introducing-medchembench",
        "source": "OpenAI",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-20T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-22T17:48:44.944Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E9",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "While measuring the benchmark for structure components, Astra earned 95.4% of the available credit at xhigh.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://openai.com/index/introducing-medchembench",
        "source": "OpenAI",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-20T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-22T17:48:44.944Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E10",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Across the full benchmark, Astra earned 83.3% of the available credit at the shared xhigh setting, compared with 82.0% for GPT‑6.1 Sol, 75.1% for GPT‑6.1 Terra, and 58.2% for GPT‑5.6 Sol.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://openai.com/index/introducing-medchembench",
        "source": "OpenAI",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-20T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-22T17:48:44.944Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E11",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Where selection and prediction remain difficult, Astra earned 95.4% of the available structure credit at xhigh, but only about half the credit for selecting compounds and predicting numerical properties.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://openai.com/index/introducing-medchembench",
        "source": "OpenAI",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-20T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-22T17:48:44.944Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E12",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "While the benchmark evaluates reasoning from historical evidence rather than real-world drug discovery, its results help identify where models are advancing and where challenges remain.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://openai.com/index/introducing-medchembench",
        "source": "OpenAI",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-20T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-22T17:48:44.944Z"
      }
